Long time reader, first time poster. "Love your show."

After the end of the November /dev/null tournament (during which I
finally ascended a wizard; mit_rax if you read scorefiles obsessively
or something) I decided to relax ("relax") by playing a few random
games of Slash'EM.  The first couple I roll up are strange things like
"ice mages" and "vampire slayers;" I learned the hard way that the early
game in Slash'EM is much less forgiving of my typical "ditch pet, get to
level 4 as quickly as possible" strategy. On my fourth or fifth game,
I get a Samurai, and I think to myself, "OK, I can probably get this
one to Minetown at least, I've got armor and a bow to start off with."
Using a bow requires a very different play style than I am used to, 
but I was pretty happy with my results, and all set to try playing with
ranged attacks. 

Then I tripped on a wand of wishing on DL 3. Not knowing anything about
Slash'EM specifically, I wished for standard things I would have wanted
in nethack; +3 blessed silver dragon scale mail, +3 blessed fixed cloak
of magic resistance, +3 blessed fixed boots of speed, +3 blessed Frost
Brand---note that I forgot to say fixed! This cost me roughly every potion
of oil ever---and an amulet of lifesaving. (Incidentally, every item I
asked for +3 came out +3. Is this a difference from vanilla or just 
incredible luck?)

I carried on with my original plan of: 

 * Shoot at things
 * Frost Brand them when they get close
 * Cautiously try to make my way to Minetown

until I made it to Minetown (not surprisingly), where I discovered
a coaligned altar, another wand of wishing, and a bag of holding. So
much for relaxing! I kitted myself out pretty nicely, wishing for a
couple of magic markers and blanking lots of stupid scrolls to get to
AC -30something, sacrificed to get Snickersnee, and then #twoweaponed
Frost Brand and Snickersnee. This made my character more or less 
obscene, though I had fewer hit points than I might have liked. Still,
with three blessed amulets of lifesaving, I felt like I was pretty safe.

And for a long time, I was! I lost one amulet of life saving to
discovering that soldiers in Slash'EM have assault rifles and frag
grenades, but didn't lose the second until a crystal golem in Vecna's lair
taught me that sometimes 200 HP _isn't_ enough. After that, I collected
all the gold from Medusa to DL 1 and brought it to my coaligned priest
and donated my way down to a -51 AC. Woohoo. Invulnerable, I thought!
Then I thought again. No, not invulnerable. I would really like to
get some more levels and also to genocide L and ; (; and I have never
gotten along, really, we had a bad experience a few years back...) The
one thing I had gotten none of except through wishes were magic markers,
and when I wished for them, I spent them getting +7 Frost Brand and +7
Snickersnee and an obscene AC instead of scrolls of genocide, which I
hadn't seen until late in the game. (First one went towards h, which
after reading about Slash'EM mind flayers may have been a mistake.)

I had a wand of polymorph and a few unicorn horns, and thought "Hmm, maybe
I should polypile for magic markers." But then I said "Wait, One-Eyed
Sam has like four of them, plus other things I'd rather like to have! I
can sacrifice my way back into good standing --- and it's not a crime if
my pet does it!" But how to get a pet in there? I at this point had three
monadic or movadic or whichever devas kicking around destroying everything
for me, but they wouldn't go in the portal, so I thought "I will wait
for something to spawn and then tame it." As best I can tell, this is
a reasonable plan; kitten shows up, throw it a tripe ration, awesome.

OK, I think to myself, now I just need my kitten to become more awesome.
Zap. Ghoul queen. Muahaha! It has queen in the name, it must be good! I
walk it over towards Sam and his minions. It kind of sits there, taciturn.
Well crap, apparently it is not more awesome. I get distracted by my cat,
lifting my keys off of my keyboard, and then put them down and zap again.
But "u" is the direction of my ghoul queen, and "y" is the direction
of my shopkeeper, and I am burdened by all of the loot I was planning
to walk out with (stupid, if only because there was no good reason to),
and my right hand was off my one key...

One-Eyed Sam is enraged, and beheads me in one turn. I come back,
and panic.  I'm not sure there was anything I could have done; I only
had one move before I got beheaded again. What I did was take a step back,
which clearly didn't work. Things I've considered since:

 * Scroll or wand of teleport. I kind of assume the shop is a no-teleport
   level, but I hadn't actually tested, and hey, better to go down trying
   (or stopping to check a spoiler at least).
 * Polymorph myself into something that couldn't be beheaded? I didn't
   have poly control but it would have been worth a shot. Though I guess
   I would just have ended up a silver dragon...
 * Whack him with my two swords? Probably wouldn't have killed him, but 
   was more likely to have done so than running away...
 * Rub magic lamp, ask for cockatrice corpse? If the beheading attack
   always works, this would be no good, but if I just happened to get
   unlucky, this would have worked on the second turn, I expect.
 * Could I have disarmed him? How does that even work? I didn't use any
   of my new #techniques or other extended commands, figuring "Freeze.
   Slice." was a pretty sufficient strategy up until that point.

In retrospect, the right thing to do would have been poly the pet into 
something tough enough, then stand back with a bow or wands and see what 
happened; I could have determined pet toughness on some of Sam's pets 
rather than on Sam himself (if I had polymorphed one of the minions by
accident, I might be in for a special treat, but at least not a special
instakill treat). Of course, the obvious way to not have this YASD is not
to make the typo, but even beyond that, had I played that room safer, I 
think I would have had better protection from the user error.

It made me really sad to have wasted about 40 hours on this game (I 
play slowly) until I realized (1) that I had learned something and (2)
perhaps more importantly, if I considered the things I had wasted time
on in my life, this was noise. :) I hope the story entertains (and 
possibly, through commentary, educates myself and others).

